    "body": "By Charlotte Goldstone\n10 November 2026\nWhat do the numbers tell us about the global container shipping market in Q3 26? In this special episode of The Loadstar Podcast , we team up with Container Trades Statistics (CTS) CEO Nigel Pusey to unpack the latest data and explore the forces shaping global trade.\nJoined by The Loadstar’ s managing editor, Gavin van Marle, we examine another quarter of record-breaking container volumes, the continued strength of Far East exports, and the changing dynamics across the transpacific and secondary markets, including South America and Sub-Saharan Africa.\nWe also explore the growing impact of port congestion, as typhoons and operational disruption put further pressure on already stretched supply chains, plus the contrasting developments in the Middle East, with increasing returns to Red Sea transits and continued uncertainty around the Strait of Hormuz.\nFinally, we revisit the predictions made in our Q2 episode to see how they measured up, before asking Nigel and Gavin to look ahead and share their forecasts for the coming months.\nFrom trade volumes and pricing trends to geopolitical disruption and shifting tradelanes, we put the Q3 container shipping market under the microscope.\nClick here to receive an email notification every time we release a podcast.\nThis article is © The Loadstar. Reproduction, rewriting, or derivative use requires a license. Contact [email protected] for licensing enquiries.",
